---
import Prose from '../layouts/Prose.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---
<Prose
  title="About CabSnap"
  description="CabSnap is built by Nuvol Holdings LLC in Spotswood, NJ. A receipt app for people who buy their own fuel."
  path="/about"
  heading="About"
>
  <p>
    CabSnap is a receipt capture app for owner-operators, lease operators, and
    1099 drivers. You photograph a receipt, the app reads it and files it, and
    it stays readable long after the paper version has faded.
  </p>

  <h2>Why it exists</h2>
  <p>
    Nearly every receipt a driver collects is thermal paper — fuel, scale tickets,
    truck stop slips. Thermal paper does not survive a summer in a cab. By the time
    anyone sits down to sort it out, a meaningful share of the year's spending is a
    stack of blank slips.
  </p>
  <p>
    That money was already spent. The only thing lost is the proof.
  </p>

  <h2>What we deliberately don't do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Mileage tracking.</strong> Good apps already exist for this. We would rather do one thing properly.</li>
    <li><strong>Tax advice.</strong> We are a recordkeeping tool. What you can deduct is a question for your tax preparer.</li>
    <li><strong>iOS.</strong> Android only for now. We would rather say so than imply otherwise.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who's behind it</h2>
  <p>
    CabSnap is a product of {SITE.company}, based in {SITE.companyCity}.
    Questions, problems, or feedback go to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>,
    and a person reads them.
  </p>

  <div class="note">
    <strong>On reviews and testimonials:</strong> you will not find star ratings,
    download counts, or customer quotes on this site. Not because there is nothing
    to say, but because inventing them is what every other app does and drivers
    can tell. When there are real reviews on the Play Store, they will speak for
    themselves there.
  </div>
</Prose>
